{"status":"ready","content":"Let the sample be $x = \\{25, 10, 0, 9, -1, -14, -21\\}$.\r\nThe number of observations is $n = 7$.\r\n\r\nFirst, we compute the sample mean, $\\bar{x}$:\r\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{\\sum x_i}{n}$\r\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 0 + 9 + (-1) + (-14) + (-21)}{7}$\r\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 9 - 1 - 14 - 21}{7}$\r\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{44 - 36}{7}$\r\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{8}{7}$\r\n\r\nNext, we compute the deviations from the mean, $(x_i - \\bar{x})$:\r\n$25 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{175 - 8}{7} = \\frac{167}{7}$\r\n$10 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{70 - 8}{7} = \\frac{62}{7}$\r\n$0 - \\frac{8}{7} = -\\frac{8}{7}$\r\n$9 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{63 - 8}{7} = \\frac{55}{7}$\r\n$-1 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-7 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{15}{7}$\r\n$-14 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-98 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{106}{7}$\r\n$-21 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-147 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{155}{7}$\r\n\r\nNow, we square these deviations, $(x_i - \\bar{x})^2$:\r\n$(\\frac{167}{7})^2 = \\frac{27889}{49}$\r\n$(\\frac{62}{7})^2 = \\frac{3844}{49}$\r\n$(-\\frac{8}{7})^2 = \\frac{64}{49}$\r\n$(\\frac{55}{7})^2 = \\frac{3025}{49}$\r\n$(-\\frac{15}{7})^2 = \\frac{225}{49}$\r\n$(-\\frac{106}{7})^2 = \\frac{11236}{49}$\r\n$(-\\frac{155}{7})^2 = \\frac{24025}{49}$\r\n\r\nThen, we sum the squared deviations:\r\n$\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{27889 + 3844 + 64 + 3025 + 225 + 11236 + 24025}{49}$\r\n$\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{70308}{49}$\r\n\r\nNext, we compute the sample variance, $s^2$:\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2}{n-1}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{70308}{49}}{7-1}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{70308}{49}}{6}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308}{49 \\times 6}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308}{294}$\r\n$s^2 = 239.142857...$\r\n\r\nAlternatively, we can use the formula $s^2 = \\frac{\\sum x_i^2 - \\frac{(\\sum x_i)^2}{n}}{n-1}$.\r\nFirst, calculate $\\sum x_i^2$:\r\n$25^2 = 625$\r\n$10^2 = 100$\r\n$0^2 = 0$\r\n$9^2 = 81$\r\n$(-1)^2 = 1$\r\n$(-14)^2 = 196$\r\n$(-21)^2 = 441$\r\n$\\sum x_i^2 = 625 + 100 + 0 + 81 + 1 + 196 + 441 = 1444$\r\nWe already computed $\\sum x_i = 8$.\r\n$(\\sum x_i)^2 = 8^2 = 64$.\r\n$\\frac{(\\sum x_i)^2}{n} = \\frac{64}{7}$.\r\n\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{64}{7}}{7-1}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{1444 \\times 7 - 64}{7}}{6}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{10108 - 64}{7 \\times 6}$\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{10044}{42}$\r\n$s^2 = 239.142857...$\r\n\r\nNow, we compute the sample standard deviation, $s$:\r\n$s = \\sqrt{s^2}$\r\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{10044}{42}}$\r\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{1674}{7}}$\r\n$s \\approx \\sqrt{239.142857...}$\r\n$s \\approx 15.464245$\r\n\r\nLet's double check the sum of squared deviations calculation to ensure no arithmetic errors.\r\n$\\bar{x} = 8/7$.\r\n$x_i$: 25, 10, 0, 9, -1, -14, -21\r\n$x_i - \\bar{x}$: $167/7$, $62/7$, $-8/7$, $55/7$, $-15/7$, $-106/7$, $-155/7$\r\n$(x_i - \\bar{x})^2$: $27889/49$, $3844/49$, $64/49$, $3025/49$, $225/49$, $11236/49$, $24025/49$\r\nSum of squared deviations numerator: $27889 + 3844 + 64 + 3025 + 225 + 11236 + 24025 = 70308$.\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308/49}{6} = \\frac{70308}{294} = \\frac{11718}{49}$.\r\nLet's recompute using the second formula:\r\n$\\sum x_i = 8$.\r\n$\\sum x_i^2 = 625+100+0+81+1+196+441 = 1444$.\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{8^2}{7}}{7-1} = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{64}{7}}{6} = \\frac{\\frac{1444 \\times 7 - 64}{7}}{6} = \\frac{10108 - 64}{42} = \\frac{10044}{42} = \\frac{1674}{7}$.\r\n\r\nAh, there was a calculation error in the sum of squares.\r\n$s^2 = \\frac{1674}{7}$\r\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{1674}{7}} = \\sqrt{239.142857...} \\approx 15.464245$.\r\n\r\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{15.464}$.\r\n","path":"responses/gemini-2-5-flash-lite/livebench-065-math.txt","size":3266,"mtime":1779368141}